# Discerning Teaching Through Scripture

Christian learning involves more than collecting ideas. It calls us to listen carefully, read faithfully, and let the whole witness of Scripture shape our understanding.

## Begin with the passage

When a sermon, book, or online post quotes a verse, take time to read the surrounding passage. Notice who is speaking, who is being addressed, and what question or situation is in view. A sentence separated from its context can sound as if it supports a claim the larger passage does not make.

## Compare interpretation with the wider story

Ask how a proposed interpretation relates to the chapter, the book, and the central message of Scripture. Consider whether the teacher distinguishes clearly between what the text says and what the teacher concludes from it. Faithful study welcomes careful questions and does not rely on dramatic claims in place of sound explanation.

## Learn in community

Discuss difficult passages with trusted pastors, faculty, and fellow believers who are willing to study patiently. A teachable spirit helps us receive correction, acknowledge uncertainty, and grow in wisdom. The goal is not to win an argument, but to understand God’s Word more faithfully and live it with love.
